@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Push notifications
+
+Push notifications to browsers work out of the box in development: without `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` in the environment, Fizzy generates a key pair on first boot and keeps it in `tmp/vapid_key.pem`. Turn notifications on for your browser from the notification settings, then act as another user to receive one. Browsers only deliver pushes on secure origins and `localhost`.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
