 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can push notifications to people's phones and desktops through their browsers, so that whatever lands in their notification tray also reaches the devices they've turned notifications on for.
+Browsers require pushes to be signed with a [VAPID](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8292) key pair, which you provide as:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+You can generate a pair by running `bin/rails push:vapid_keys` in a checkout of Fizzy, or with `docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bin/rails push:vapid_keys`.
+Keep the same pair for the lifetime of your instance: changing it means everyone has to turn notifications on again.
+Without a key pair, push notifications are simply left out of the notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
