 - `SMTP_USERNAME` & `SMTP_PASSWORD` should be valid credentials for your SMTP server. If you're using a 3rd-party service here, consult their documentation for what to use.
+
+Optionally, Fizzy can push notifications to people's phones and desktops through their browsers. To turn that on, uncomment `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` under `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml`, and add the pair to `.kamal/secrets`. You can run `bin/rails push:vapid_keys` to create a suitable pair. Keep the same pair for the lifetime of your instance: changing it means everyone has to turn notifications on again.
+
 Once you've made all those changes, commit them to your fork so they're saved.
 
